1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,351
Welcome to Classroom Screen Sharing. Teachers use a website, and
students use a Chrome extension. Your

2
00:00:06,351 --> 00:00:12,702
teacher or institution must run the classroom backend and dashboard.
Installing the extension alone does not

3
00:00:12,702 --> 00:00:19,053
create a hosted classroom. This guided demonstration uses sample content
and illustrations, not a recording of

4
00:00:19,053 --> 00:00:21,435
an accepted native screen capture dialog.

5
00:00:22,935 --> 00:00:28,609
Teachers first start the backend and dashboard using the project
instructions. Give the server a trusted

6
00:00:28,609 --> 00:00:34,283
HTTPS address reachable from student laptops. Sign into the teacher
website and create a course and

7
00:00:34,283 --> 00:00:39,957
session. Share the server address and the eight character classroom
code. The same Wi-Fi network can

8
00:00:39,957 --> 00:00:45,630
be used, but localhost on a student laptop points to that student
laptop, not to the

9
00:00:45,630 --> 00:00:45,985
teacher.

10
00:00:47,485 --> 00:00:53,088
After the extension is published, students install it from its official
Chrome Web Store listing and

11
00:00:53,088 --> 00:00:58,691
pin it to the toolbar. Click the icon and choose Open sharing controls.
Before publication, an

12
00:00:58,691 --> 00:01:04,293
administrator can build the project and use Chrome developer mode to
load the extension dist folder

13
00:01:04,293 --> 00:01:07,795
unpacked. Keep the sharing controls and Chrome open while sharing.

14
00:01:09,295 --> 00:01:15,431
Enter the exact HTTPS server address and classroom code provided by your
teacher. Click Check classroom

15
00:01:15,431 --> 00:01:21,566
slash join and review Chrome server access permission. Grant access only
to a server you trust.

16
00:01:21,566 --> 00:01:27,702
In a code-only classroom, also enter your name and student ID. If your
school requires Google

17
00:01:27,702 --> 00:01:30,386
sign-in, continue using the Google button instead.

18
00:01:31,886 --> 00:01:38,053
When Google login is required, click Sign in with Google and join.
Choose your managed school

19
00:01:38,053 --> 00:01:44,219
account. The backend verifies the Google identity and enforces the exact
allowed domain list. Other accounts

20
00:01:44,219 --> 00:01:50,386
are rejected. Personal Gmail accounts work only if the administrator
explicitly allows gmail dot com. The

21
00:01:50,386 --> 00:01:56,553
teacher sees your verified name and email. This guide illustrates the
step; an actual Google login

22
00:01:56,553 --> 00:01:58,866
requires the institution’s configured OAuth client.

23
00:02:00,366 --> 00:02:06,149
Before sharing, read the disclosure in the controls. Your chosen screen
or window will be transmitted

24
00:02:06,149 --> 00:02:11,932
to your classroom server for the teacher to view. The teacher may enable
periodic screenshot recording

25
00:02:11,932 --> 00:02:17,715
and optional archive uploads to the teacher’s Google Drive. Anything
visible in the selected source can

26
00:02:17,715 --> 00:02:21,691
appear in those images. Close private content, then check the
acknowledgement.

27
00:02:23,191 --> 00:02:29,551
Click Start Sharing. Chrome opens its own native permission picker.
Select the screen or application window

28
00:02:29,551 --> 00:02:35,912
you intend to share, and confirm in Chrome. The illustration here is not
the native permission

29
00:02:35,912 --> 00:02:42,273
dialog. This product never chooses the source silently. No webcam,
microphone or audio capture is requested.

30
00:02:42,273 --> 00:02:47,441
On a Mac, Chrome may also need Screen Recording permission in system
settings.

31
00:02:48,941 --> 00:02:55,310
You can now switch to VS Code, Jupyter, PyCharm or another application.
The selected source continues

32
00:02:55,310 --> 00:03:01,680
sharing while available and while Chrome’s authorized capture session
remains active. Keep the extension controls open.

33
00:03:01,680 --> 00:03:08,049
A minimized or closed application window may stop updating depending on
the operating system. Share the

34
00:03:08,049 --> 00:03:12,030
full screen if needed. Watch the sharing and recording indicators.

35
00:03:13,530 --> 00:03:18,918
On the teacher dashboard, student cards show the images received from
connected extensions. Search by name

36
00:03:18,918 --> 00:03:24,306
or student ID and check connection status and the last image timestamp.
Click a card to

37
00:03:24,306 --> 00:03:29,693
request a larger, higher quality view with more readable code text.
Close it or press Escape

38
00:03:29,693 --> 00:03:35,081
to return to overview. Up to two distinct students can be focused at
once. The dashboard

39
00:03:35,081 --> 00:03:39,795
image in this guide is from a browser test with clearly marked synthetic
content.

40
00:03:41,295 --> 00:03:47,740
Recording is separate from live monitoring and starts off in a new
classroom. If appropriate for

41
00:03:47,740 --> 00:03:54,186
the class, explain your institution’s policy and enable periodic
screenshot recording. The default is one changed

42
00:03:54,186 --> 00:04:00,631
screenshot every twenty seconds, with a configurable interval. The
system records screenshots, not continuous video. Open

43
00:04:00,631 --> 00:04:07,076
Playback to choose a student and review the original timestamps.
Optional Google Drive uploads use ZIP

44
00:04:07,076 --> 00:04:07,479
batches.

45
00:04:08,979 --> 00:04:15,407
Students can stop immediately using Stop Sharing in the extension
controls, the toolbar popup or Chrome’s

46
00:04:15,407 --> 00:04:21,835
sharing indicator. Closing the extension controls also stops capture.
Teachers end the classroom when the lesson

47
00:04:21,835 --> 00:04:28,264
finishes. The old joining code becomes invalid. Short network
interruptions can reconnect using the existing authorized

48
00:04:28,264 --> 00:04:34,692
stream. After thirty seconds without the server, capture stops and the
student must deliberately start sharing

49
00:04:34,692 --> 00:04:35,093
again.

50
00:04:36,593 --> 00:04:43,291
Before teaching, test real capture on two devices, including source
selection, switching applications, focused viewing, recording

51
00:04:43,291 --> 00:04:49,988
playback, Stop Sharing and ending the classroom. Confirm HTTPS works on
student devices and approved Google

52
00:04:49,988 --> 00:04:56,686
accounts can join if required. Review the student and teacher guides.
The demonstration video is ready

53
00:04:56,686 --> 00:05:02,128
to share as instructions; it does not replace that real hardware
acceptance test.
